But the big issue: schedule. As of 03-09, no approval. Even B with Reference lead 4 days: order 03-09 → delivery 03-13 (conservative) → install/cal 03-14–03-16 → observation 03-17–03-30 = misses Day 28 by one day. If inclusive: delivery 03-12 → install 03-13–03-15 → observation 03-16–03-29 exactly meets, but only if approval and order happen today and the R3 verification can be completed within install/cal (3 days) and no other delay. That's not a credible plan; it's a knife-edge. And the field-validation Echo result suggests additional R3 verification needed. Also there's no approval, so "today" can't be assumed.

