So under the proposed 6000, only B base and C fit; B resilience doesn't. B base has no spare battery/logger; 220 headroom.

But B base under 6000 requires Echo at S1, and Echo S1 low-RH/temperature verification. Also mixed-model cross-calibration. B base has no S1 logger (network stable, so not strictly required, but no offline storage). B base 220 headroom.

