Wait — should we say R4 is definitively failed? Let's be precise: As of 2026-03-09T09:10Z, no approval exists. The latest order date to preserve a 14-day Reference observation ending by Day 28 was 2026-03-08 under the conservative convention. It has passed. Under the inclusive convention, 2026-03-09 is the last possible day, but that requires approval and order today and no verification delay; and R5 approval is absent. R3 pre-deployment verification must be completed before deployment; if it takes time, it pushes start later. So R4 is not demonstrated and is at best a zero-buffer edge case, i.e., effectively at risk/failed. I'll say "R4 is not met on the plan's own conservative gate; it is only theoretically reachable under an inclusive lead-time interpretation with same-day approval, which is not present. Therefore R4 cannot be relied on." That's honest.

