Thus the correct conclusion is: cannot approve; the only evidence-credible design (Reference at S2/S3) cannot meet R4 on the current date; a requirement change/rebase is an operator decision, not ours. We can propose a "conditional design" for if the operator rebases the calendar or grants an exception. But R4 is critical and binding; we must not manufacture feasibility. We should record the design that would be proposed under an approved rebase, with all conditions.

